  "details": "1. Open scaling radial. \n\n2. Attempt to set radial to a value close to one of the cardinal directions\n\n3. Note how the radial will snap to those directions. \n\nI heard from someone else in the instance that this may be a VR specific issue as radials behave slightly differently on Desktop but I have not had a chance to try. \n\nNot entirely sure if this is considered a bug but it makes it impossible to fine tune your height around those positions it snaps to. In testing that's about 0.1m in both directions around the snapping point. \n\nWill try to do further testing on an avatar w/ a default height close to one of those snapping points to see if both snapping points conflict with each other.",
